several people homeless tonight after a  large fire at a mobile home park in  henderson  it started late sunday night at the alta  vista park near warm springs and lake  mead  madison kimbrough talked with those  living there about how the fire has  affected them  denise residents here at the alta vista  community describe themselves as a  family and last night's fire which you  can see behind me  spread quickly affecting the entire  mobile home park  i heard what sound like fireworks i  heard them louder and louder  i see my currents light up when it was  going on  i looked out the back window there's a  ball of fire i heard  explosions and stuff like that then i  come around the corner and i see the  fire over here  flames erupted at this mobile home park  in henderson sunday night causing the  whole park to evacuate  the cause of the fire is still unknown  but residents say  fireworks have been going off in the  area as of late  fireworks are common in this area i hear  them all the time the fire displaced  several residents and according to  henderson and clark county fire  multiple cars were damaged and eight  mobile homes are now demolished  but luckily no injuries to residents  have been reported  we couldn't come back in the park so we  all had to go  to the to the school right across the  street and we waited there until 6 a.m  power was restored to the park early  monday evening donny probert has lived  in this community for 15 years so he  wants to do something to help  i would like to get a fundraiser to go  you know for all these people that are  displaced  his commute is pretty tight and it will  happen  again the henderson fire department has  not said what caused the blaze just  yet but the red cross is assisting these  families with anything that they need a  really tight community here  at this mobile home park we really wish  them all the best reporting live in  henderson madison kimbrough 8 news now
 

